SWEET dev overlay v2 (patch 0154, on top of 0117): zlib-compressed entries, bounded streaming inflate.
Archive version 2 stores each entry as u64 inflated size + one zlib stream (tools/mkdevoverlay.py --compress); version 1 is unchanged and still accepted.
Uses libkern inflate (libkern/zlib/inflate.c, option zlib; _inflate/_inflateInit_/_inflateEnd are in the built kernel: llvm-nm of
localbuild/out/kernel.development.sweet). Memory: two 1 MiB chunks plus ~40 KiB of inflate state; the inflated file is never held whole.
Bounds: stored length <= 48 MiB, inflated size per entry and sum <= 40 MiB (else the archive is refused whole); per entry a verify pass
(stream well-formed, exactly the declared size, no trailing bytes, crc32 over the inflated bytes) runs BEFORE anything is written, then
compare and write passes re-inflate (the write pass re-checks the crc and never renames on a mismatch). Hardware-writing path (writes userdata files): review docs/reviews/devoverlay-z-1.md SAFE WITH CONDITIONS; round-1 findings 1-3 fixed, build and device proof pending.

