+ *   version 2 (patch 0154): "size" is the STORED length and the stored data is u64 inflated size (<= 40 MiB)
+ *     | one zlib stream (RFC 1950, libkern inflate, streamed in 1 MiB chunks, never held whole). crc32 is over the INFLATED
+ *     bytes. Limits: stored length <= 48 MiB, sum of inflated sizes <= 40 MiB (else the archive is refused whole); an
+ *     entry whose stream is bad, ends early, yields more or fewer bytes than declared, has trailing bytes or a bad crc
+ *     is refused alone, before anything is written (a verify pass, then a compare pass and a write pass).
  * The kernel never trusts the archive: the whole structure is walked first (magic, version, count,
  * every length against the remaining bytes, no overflow) and nothing is written if that fails.
  * A bad crc or path only skips that entry.
